WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:08.960
So now, the first thing that we have learned that we can go and have like one query, write something

00:08.960 --> 00:09.520
like this.

00:09.520 --> 00:11.360
Select star from customers.

00:11.400 --> 00:12.840
Now this is one query.

00:12.840 --> 00:14.920
And in the output we have one results.

00:14.920 --> 00:20.760
But did you know that in SQL we can have like multiple queries and multiple results in one go.

00:20.760 --> 00:22.280
So we can do everything together.

00:22.320 --> 00:26.600
Like for example let's say I'm selecting as well the data from orders.

00:27.200 --> 00:28.720
So that means we have two queries.

00:28.760 --> 00:33.800
And now if you go and execute what can happens you will get two result grids.

00:33.800 --> 00:39.280
The first result grid is for the first query and the second one is for the second query.

00:39.280 --> 00:42.800
So with that you can do multiple queries in the same window.

00:42.800 --> 00:47.400
And with that the results can be split into multiple window depend how many queries you have.

00:47.440 --> 00:53.360
And usually in SQL you might find that by the end of each query there is a semicolon like this.

00:53.360 --> 00:55.600
So at the end of the first query I have semicolon.

00:55.600 --> 00:59.280
And for the second query we have as well at the end another semicolon.

00:59.280 --> 01:04.840
For the SQL server it is not a must, but for other databases, if you have multiple queries in one

01:04.840 --> 01:07.880
execution, you must separate them with a semicolon.

01:07.880 --> 01:09.680
And with that, the database can understands.

01:09.720 --> 01:15.010
Okay, this is the end of the first query and this is the end of the second query.

01:15.010 --> 01:17.650
So you have like separations between queries.

01:21.490 --> 01:21.850
Okay.

01:21.850 --> 01:24.250
Now moving on to another cool thing in SQL.

01:24.290 --> 01:27.890
Now what if we don't want to query the data inside our tables.

01:27.890 --> 01:32.330
We would like to show a static value from us from the one that is writing the query.

01:32.330 --> 01:37.210
And this is very practical if you are like practicing and you want to check something using a value

01:37.210 --> 01:39.330
from you, not from the tables.

01:39.330 --> 01:40.610
So how we can do that?

01:40.610 --> 01:41.610
It is very simple.

01:41.610 --> 01:47.650
We're going to write select and then now after that, instead of having a column name you can go and

01:47.650 --> 01:49.610
add any value like one two, three.

01:49.610 --> 01:53.810
So it is just a number and we do not specify after that any table.

01:53.810 --> 01:54.970
So we leave it like this.

01:54.970 --> 01:58.130
Select 123 and we don't need to use the from clause.

01:58.130 --> 02:01.130
So now if you go and execute it you will get 123.

02:01.130 --> 02:02.690
So this is a static value.

02:02.690 --> 02:07.170
And of course you can go and rename the column like static number.

02:07.610 --> 02:08.890
So execute it again.

02:08.890 --> 02:10.610
So with that we have a static value.

02:10.610 --> 02:13.210
And you can go and add anything like string as well.

02:13.210 --> 02:16.970
So let's say hello as static for example string.

02:16.970 --> 02:18.450
So let's go and execute.

02:18.490 --> 02:19.690
And we have two queries.

02:19.690 --> 02:21.970
The second one you can see our static value.

02:22.010 --> 02:22.370
Hello.

02:22.370 --> 02:27.860
So in queries we can add values from us not only selecting data from the queries, but of course you

02:27.860 --> 02:33.340
can go and mix stuff so we can have like in one query, data from the database and static data from

02:33.380 --> 02:33.740
us.

02:33.740 --> 02:34.900
So let me show you what I mean.

02:34.900 --> 02:40.860
Let's go over here and say select and let's go and get, for example, the ID the first name from the

02:40.860 --> 02:41.420
table.

02:41.460 --> 02:43.100
Customers like this.

02:43.100 --> 02:46.300
So with that we can see we are getting data from the database.

02:46.300 --> 02:52.060
But now I can go and add something from me new customer and we can call it customer type.

02:52.660 --> 02:53.980
So now what is going on here.

02:53.980 --> 02:57.220
Two columns from the database and one column from us.

02:57.220 --> 02:58.380
It is the static one.

02:58.380 --> 03:01.700
So if you go and execute it you can see for the ID and the first name.

03:01.700 --> 03:03.420
Those data comes from the database.

03:03.460 --> 03:08.580
But for each record we are always getting the same static value new customer, new customer and so on.

03:08.580 --> 03:11.340
So this piece of information comes from the query.

03:11.380 --> 03:13.540
It is not stored inside the database.

03:13.540 --> 03:17.660
And those two informations come from the stored data inside the database.

03:17.660 --> 03:19.100
So this is really cool thing.

03:19.260 --> 03:23.700
You can add few informations from you and you can get the data from the database.

03:23.700 --> 03:25.340
This is the static values.

03:29.220 --> 03:33.420
Okay one more cool thing that I want to show you is that if you have a query like this, you are selecting

03:33.420 --> 03:35.140
from table and filtering the data.

03:35.140 --> 03:37.700
And now you would like not to execute the whole thing.

03:37.700 --> 03:40.260
You would like to execute only a part of this query.

03:40.260 --> 03:44.140
So now sometimes as you are writing a query, you don't want to execute the whole thing.

03:44.140 --> 03:46.420
You want to execute only a part of the query.

03:46.460 --> 03:50.820
Like for example, I would like to see all the customers again in this query without this filter.

03:50.820 --> 03:55.100
So instead of removing it, I then query and then again adding it.

03:55.100 --> 04:00.860
What you can do, you can highlight what you want without now the filter and execute so that the database

04:00.860 --> 04:02.900
can execute exactly what you highlighted.

04:02.900 --> 04:05.660
And now as you can see, I'm getting all the customers without the filter.

04:05.660 --> 04:11.020
And if you don't highlight anything and execute, what can happen is SQL can execute the whole thing

04:11.020 --> 04:12.020
inside the editor.

04:12.020 --> 04:16.340
And this is really nice if you want to query another table quickly in the same editor, like we want

04:16.340 --> 04:21.700
to select everything from the orders just quickly, so you can highlight only this query and execute.

04:21.700 --> 04:26.620
And with that, SQL is ignoring everything else and only executing what I'm highlighting.

04:26.620 --> 04:27.540
And this is really nice.

04:27.540 --> 04:29.460
It gives us like speed and dynamic.

04:29.460 --> 04:32.260
And you can find me doing that a lot in the course.

04:32.260 --> 04:34.020
So this is really nice okay my friends.

04:34.020 --> 04:39.700
So with that we have learned the basics about SQL query, the basic components of the Select statements.

04:39.700 --> 04:42.780
And with that we can talk to our database in order to get data.

04:42.820 --> 04:46.820
Now in the next chapter we're going to learn how to define the structure of our database.

04:46.820 --> 04:49.780
So we're going to learn the data definition language DDL.

04:49.820 --> 04:50.540
So let's go.
